# Ctrl+C at the bash prompt declines it and interrupts the turn in one
# key press, as in Claude Code. Unlike Esc on this same prompt
# (bash-esc-decline.steps), there is no "✕ Declined …" note: the decline
# goes through PromptState.cancelAll, not finishTool, so only the turn's
# own "■ Interrupted" line shows.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/permissions-esc-decline.yaml

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE deploy to production
KEY enter
WAITFOR /approval needed/ 20
SHOT bash-prompt
EXPECT /curl https:\/\/example\.invalid\/deploy/
KEY ctrl+c
WAIT 1
SHOT after-ctrlc
EXPECT_NOT /approval needed/
EXPECT /■ Interrupted\. Tell kiln what to do instead\./
EXPECT_NOT /✕ Declined/
EXPECT_NOT /Okay, I won.t run it/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
